  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe donor's tax rate under the TRAIN law is six percent (6%) on the total gifts exceeding Two hundred fifty thousand pesos (₱250,000) made during the calendar year.\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 99 of the NIRC specifies that the donor's tax is computed based on the total gifts made in excess of the annual exemption threshold of ₱250,000. This means that any gifts made up to this amount are exempt from donor's tax, while gifts exceeding this threshold are subject to the 6% tax rate.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, individuals making gifts should be aware that they can give up to ₱250,000 in a calendar year without incurring any donor's tax liability. However, any amount above this threshold will be taxed at 6%, which necessitates proper record-keeping and tax planning for those who frequently make substantial gifts.",
